{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 28, :comments ["<b>For a nation lost of counsel.</b> The meaning is that there is no concern lest the nation see and take admonition and say: If these, for provoking Him only a little — see what befell them, etc. — and thereby improve his deeds. And this is what it says, ״כִּי גוֹי אֹבַד עֵצוֹת״ — the meaning is that such a thing is not in its nature, and it is lost from counsels of this sort; ״וְאֵין בָּהֶם תְּבוּנָה״ to understand a matter from within a matter, as we said: ״לוּ חָכְמוּ יַשְׂכִּילוּ זֹאת״ — meaning, the fierceness of wrath that comes upon Israel — and from this they would understand their latter end, what will come about from their exaltation."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:21:29.900464905Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}